{"resource": {"name": "COVID-19 Case Disposition", "id": "wg8s-i3c7", "parent_fxf": [], "description": "This dataset provides the daily & cumulative number of COVID-19 new confirmed cases, hospitalizations, and deaths among Marin County residents (does not include San Quentin inmates). Event Date corresponds to date that each status type occurred. For Confirmed Case this is Test Date, for Hospitalized this is Hospital Admit Date, and for Death it is the Date of Death. If a person first tested positive for COVID-19 on 11/1/2020, was admitted to the hospital on 11/15/2020, and died on 11/20/2020, their data would be contained in three rows for each status and event date. Note: as of 11/2/2021 hospitalization counts no longer includes in-patient hospitalizations with a COVID-19 positive test when the patient was in the hospital for a reason other than COVID-19. This can include in-patient stays due to labor/delivery, trauma, or emergency surgery. The previous definition of COVID-19 hospitalizations, counting all in-patient hospitalizations with a COVID-19 positive test, measured the burden of disease on hospital resources, while this updated definition is a more appropriate measure of disease severity among Marin County residents. \n\nCases are lab-confirmed COVID-19 cases reported to Marin County Public Health by providers, commercial laboratories, and academic laboratories, including reporting results through the California Reportable Disease Information Exchange.</strong> A lab-confirmed case is defined as detection of SARS-CoV-2 RNA in a clinical specimen using a molecular amplification detection test. For more information about data sources and methods please reference the <u><a href=\"https://coronavirus.marinhhs.org/surveillance/faqs\">FAQs</a></u>.</p>", "attribution": null, "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2022-07-30T03:00:18.000Z", "createdAt": "2020-12-08T02:17:29.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2022-04-07T19:20:31.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2022-07-30T03:00:18.000Z", "columns_name": ["Last Updated", "Status", "Cumulative Case Count", "New Confirmed Cases", "Event Date"], "columns_field_name": ["last_updated", "status", "cumulative_case_count", "new_confirmed_cases", "test_date"], "columns_datatype": ["Calendar date", "Text", "Number", "Number", "Calendar date"], "columns_description": ["Timestamp data last updated", "Disposition of the case: Confirmed Case, Hospitalized, Death", "Cumulative count of new cases by status/disposition up to date", "Count of new cases by status/disposition per day", "Corresponds to Test Date for Confirmed Case, Hospital Admit Date for Hospitalized, and Date of Death for Death"], "columns_format": [{"view": "date_time"}, {}, {}, {}, {"view": "date"}], "provenance": "official", "lens_view_type": "tabular", "lens_display_type": "table", "blob_mime_type": null, "hide_from_data_json": false, "publication_date": "2020-12-11T19:13:58.000Z"}, "classification": {"categories": ["health", "infrastructure", "environment"], "tags": [], "domain_category": "Public Health", "domain_tags": ["cases", "covid-19", "disposition", "public health"], "domain_metadata": [{"key": "Dataset-Information_Department", "value": "Health & Human Services"}, {"key": "Dataset-Information_Data-Source", "value": "SQL Database"}, {"key": "Dataset-Information_Update-Frequency", "value": "Every Few Hours"}, {"key": "Dataset-Information_Geographic-Coverage", "value": "Countywide"}]}, "metadata": {"domain": "data.marincounty.org", "license": "Open Data Commons Open Database License"}, "permalink": "https://data.marincounty.org/d/wg8s-i3c7", "link": "https://data.marincounty.org/Public-Health/COVID-19-Case-Disposition/wg8s-i3c7", "owner": {"id": "ckcx-cesy", "user_type": "interactive", "display_name": "OD Marin"}, "creator": {"id": "ckcx-cesy", "user_type": "interactive", "display_name": "OD Marin"}}
{"resource": {"name": "Tax Collector ERAF Contribution", "id": "whct-xqwb", "parent_fxf": [], "description": "What is ERAF?\nIt is a mechanism, enacted in July of 1992 by the State Legislature, to shift local tax revenues from cities, counties, and special districts to a state-controlled Education Revenue Augmentation Fund. The state uses this fund to reduce their obligation to the schools. ERAF funds have been used by the State to help school and community college districts meet minimum funding requirements.\n\nWhy was ERAF created?\nProposition 13, the 1978 ballot measure capped property taxes in the state and thereby sharply diminished the property tax revenues that counties, cities, and special districts had to provide services. ERAF allowed the legislature to reallocate the property tax among local governments. In the midst of the recession in 1991-92, the State Legislature exercised this power to take city, county, and special district property taxes to fund the state government's obligation to support schools. The amount of the estimated shift for fiscal year 2010-11 and the prior two fiscal years from Marin County local agencies to ERAF is as shown below.", "attribution": null, "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2022-01-27T17:20:10.000Z", "createdAt": "2021-12-22T22:47:16.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2022-01-27T17:20:10.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2021-12-22T22:55:07.000Z", "columns_name": ["Excess ERAF", "Unique ID", "Percentage", "Fiscal Year", "Type", "Gross Contribution", "Net Contribution"], "columns_field_name": ["excess_eraf", "unique_id", "percentage", "fiscal_year", "type", "gross_contribution", "net_contribution"], "columns_datatype": ["Number", "Text", "Number", "Text", "Text", "Number", "Number"], "columns_description": ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], "columns_format": [{}, {}, {"precisionStyle": "percentage", "percentScale": "1"}, {}, {}, {}, {}], "provenance": "official", "lens_view_type": "tabular", "lens_display_type": "table", "blob_mime_type": null, "hide_from_data_json": false, "publication_date": "2021-12-22T22:55:13.000Z"}, "classification": {"categories": [], "tags": [], "domain_category": "County Government", "domain_tags": [], "domain_metadata": [{"key": "Dataset-Information_Department", "value": "Finance, Department of"}, {"key": "Dataset-Information_Data-Source", "value": "Spreadsheet, CSV"}, {"key": "Dataset-Information_Update-Frequency", "value": "Yearly"}]}, "metadata": {"domain": "data.marincounty.org"}, "permalink": "https://data.marincounty.org/d/whct-xqwb", "link": "https://data.marincounty.org/County-Government/Tax-Collector-ERAF-Contribution/whct-xqwb", "owner": {"id": "ynvb-ib52", "user_type": "interactive", "display_name": "Ashia Ismail"}, "creator": {"id": "ynvb-ib52", "user_type": "interactive", "display_name": "Ashia Ismail"}}
